    explanation: 'Catastrophic forgetting in LLM fine-tuning: (1) Mechanism: gradient descent during fine-tuning modifies the same weights that encode general knowledge — the optimization pushes toward task-specific performance at the expense of general capabilities; (2) LoRA mitigation: Low-Rank Adaptation freezes all base model weights and adds small trainable rank-decomposition matrices (A, B where weight update delta-W = BA) — only the adapter weights (typically less than 1% of parameters) are updated, preserving base model capabilities; (3) Vertex AI SFT offers LoRA fine-tuning for Gemini models — the recommended approach for domain adaptation with capability preservation; (4) EWC adds a regularization term penalizing changes to weights important for previously learned tasks (measured by Fisher information); (5) Evaluation: after fine-tuning, run MMLU or similar benchmark alongside domain benchmarks to quantify forgetting. Source: Google Professional ML Engineer exam guide, Vertex AI generative AI tuning documentation, Hu et al. (2021) LoRA: Low-Rank Adaptation of Large Language Models.',
